From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Windows with a caption are never clipped as fullscreen.

Wine clips the cursor to a foreground window that covers its monitor, for fullscreen games.
Only maximized windows with a caption were left out: Unreal Editor's window made as big as the
monitor without being maximized kept the pointer inside it (under Wayland a confined pointer, so
the desktop's panels could not be reached). Windows itself never clips; a window with a caption is
an application's window, not a fullscreen game, whatever its size.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/input.c b/dlls/win32u/input.c
index 40f076a..ab219be 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -2817,8 +2817,10 @@ BOOL clip_fullscreen_window( HWND hwnd, BOOL reset )
     style = NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE );
     if (!(style & WS_VISIBLE)) return FALSE;
     if ((style & (WS_POPUP | WS_CHILD)) == WS_CHILD) return FALSE;
-    /* maximized windows don't count as full screen */
-    if ((style & WS_MAXIMIZE) && (style & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION) return FALSE;
+    /* windows with a caption don't count as full screen, maximized or not: an application's
+     * window the user made as big as the monitor (Unreal Editor) is no fullscreen game, and
+     * clipping the cursor to it keeps the pointer from ever leaving it (the desktop's panels) */
+    if ((style & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION) return FALSE;
 
     ctx = set_thread_dpi_awareness_context( NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE );
     if (!(ret = get_present_rect( hwnd, &window_rect, get_thread_dpi() )))
